1. You receive a call from someone who is claiming to be from your bank. Right after you have received a notification from your bank alerting you that someone has tried to gain access to your account. The caller informs you are required to perform a verification process, or your account will be closed. This verification process requires to provide your account number and the 3 digits from the back of your card. What do you do?

A. Proceed and complete the verification process.
B. Ask for the caller's full name and their workplace. So you would be able to locate and hold accountable if anything happens if you proceed with the verification process.
C. End the call, contact your bank using contacts from the official website of your bank, or go to your neariest bank office.
D. None of the above.

2. The store that you have been outspoken about on social media, or the store that you like and follow on social media, or a well-known store, has sent you an email. The email informs you about the store's promotion campaign, you need to redeem the 50% discount voucher clicking the link or the email says open the pdf to see which items have 50% discount for this "special weekend". What do you do?

A. Click the link, and redeem the voucher
B. Open the pdf, and view the items
C. Check if the promotion exisit
D. Check if the email address is actually from that store.

